cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StepScope in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "StepScope: a research toolkit for post-training dynamics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Zepeng
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lexwzp0/stepscope"
abstract: >-
  StepScope compares first-order predictions with actual changes in differentiable
  observables on supported Hugging Face causal language models. It analyzes checkpoint
  pairs or controlled single optimizer steps with SFT and Open-MOPD losses using SGD
  or AdamW, and produces calibration reports and result tables. SGD steps additionally
  support source decomposition and experimental LDCL channel diagnostics.
